        "description": "<p><strong>Bards were terrible at keeping secrets. They insisted on putting them to music.</strong></p><p><em>—Tanya Huff, Sing the Four Quarters</em></p><p>Bard’s are heralds of the awe-inspiring beauty of creation. While the painter and sculptor decorate space, a Bard decorates time.</p><h3>Iconic Bards</h3><ul><li><strong>Edward Chris von Muir</strong>, <em>Final Fantasy IV</em></li><li><strong>Jaskier</strong>, <em>The Witcher</em></li><li><strong>Kvothe</strong>, <em>The Kingkiller Chronicle</em></li><li><strong>Sylvando</strong>, <em>Dragon Quest XI</em></li></ul><h3>Playing Bards</h3><p>The bard is a mid-defense, high-support class with a focus on optimizing your Group’s d20 rolls. It’s recommended that you avoid melee on most Bard builds.</p><p><strong>Action:</strong> Virtuoso<br /><strong>Move:</strong> Midline/Backline<br /><strong>Starting Pack:</strong> Musician<br /><strong>Key Stat:</strong> Presence<br /><strong>Complexity:</strong> ★★☆☆☆<br /><strong>Training:</strong> Finesse, Influence, Performance</p><h3>Class Features</h3><table class=\"NormalTable\"><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Level</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Features</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1st</p></td><td><p>Virtuoso, Well-Versed</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2nd</p></td><td><p>Overtuned (21+)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3rd</p></td><td><p>Perk</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4th</p></td><td><p>Audacity (Cd4)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5th</p></td><td><p>Perk</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6th</p></td><td><p>Overtuned (20+), Enjoy the Silence</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>7th</p></td><td><p>Perk</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>8th</p></td><td><p>Audacity (Cd6)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>9th</p></td><td><p>Perk</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>10th</p></td><td><p>Overtuned (19+), Climax</p></td></tr></tbody></table>",
        "isSpellcaster": false,
        "levelFeatures": [
          {
            "level": 1,
            "name": "Virtuoso",
            "description": "<p>You can use your Action or skip your Move to choose one of the following benefits and make a Performance Check. If you pass, your Group gains the benefit for that Round:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Inspiration:</strong> d6 bonus to Healing rolls</p></li><li><p><strong>Resolve:</strong> Favor on Saves</p></li><li><p><strong>Valor:</strong> Favor on Attack and Cast Checks</p></li></ul>",
            "statBonusPoints": 0,
